*.env
.idea/*
out/
.envrc
CLAUDE.md

# Terraform (ADR 0002 — state leaves git, it lives in Cloudflare R2).
# A committed state file let a mid-incident `git restore .` roll state back to
# a version describing servers that no longer existed.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
*.tfplan
crash.log

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — provider versions are
# pinned per module and belong in review.

# Claude Code local settings (personal, not team config).
.claude/settings.local.json

# kluster is built from source (branch feat/kluster-cli); the 11 MB binary is
# a build artefact, not infrastructure. kluster.yaml IS committed.
tools/kluster/kluster
tools/kluster/.idea/

# Editor swap files. A stale one was committed by accident in this repo once.
*.swp
*.swo

# 🔴 Holds GITHUB_CLIENT_ID/SECRET and GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET in plaintext in a
# ConfigMap (its own comment says "todo store these as k8s secrets"). GitHub push
# protection blocked a push that included it on 2026-09-21. Ignored until the
# values move into a SOPS-encrypted Secret in Phase 5 — then delete this rule,
# because the file itself should be committed once it holds no secrets.
projects/imaps/backend/manifests/configmap.yaml
